client identifier in the steps you want to connect."},"2331":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"The root in this path signs the end-entity certificate directly to simplify evaluation. Before designing an operational PKI, review the trust model and CA hierarchy."},"2332":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"File or resource"},"2333":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"Check"},"2334":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"Active root CA and `ca.pem`"},"2335":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"It is a CA certificate, is currently valid and its self-signature verifies."},"2336":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"End-entity certificate and `device.crt`"},"2337":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"It identifies `device-001`, supports client authentication and verifies against `ca.pem`."},"2338":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"Private key `device.key`"},"2339":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"Its public key matches the one included in `device.crt`."},"2340":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"These checks validate the issued material. Acceptance by a service also requires its trust, authorization and revocation configuration."},"2341":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#continue-according-to-your-goal","content":"To operate certificates, continue with Certificates and Validation."},"2342":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#continue-according-to-your-goal","content":"To manage a device identity in Lamassu, follow Manual registration. That path includes DMS preparation."},"2343":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#continue-according-to-your-goal","content":"For the device to request its certificate, prepare the DMS and EST client."},"2344":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"PKI troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting"},"2345":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose certificate issuance, OCSP and CRL."},"2346":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Issuance fails"},"2347":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"OCSP or CRL do not reflect a change"},"2348":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"The chain validates but the connection fails"},"2349":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"This guide helps a PKI operator locate issuance and status publication failures. Keep the Lamassu version, operation, CA, issuer, serial, time and returned error. Do not include private keys or tokens in diagnostics."},"2350":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"For Gateway, sign-in, pods, dependencies and messaging, see Deployment troubleshooting. For device enrollment, see EST diagnostics."},"2351":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check"},"2352":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"What to inspect"},"2353":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Next step"},"2354":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CA"},"2355":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Exists, is active and has usable dates."},"2356":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Authorities."},"2357":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Key"},"2358":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"The record has a usable private key and the engine can sign."},"2359":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Try **Sign / Verify** in KMS; check provider permissions and availability."},"2360":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CSR"},"2361":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Correct PEM and verifiable signature."},"2362":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"`openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`."},"2363":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Profile"},"2364":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Selected source, existing ID, allowed algorithm and size."},"2365":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check Profiles precedence; CA and DMS resolve differently."},"2366":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Result"},"2367":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Appropriate subject, SAN, usages and dates."},"2368":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Compare CSR, profile and certificate; successful issuance does not establish consumer acceptance."},"2369":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For unexpected certificate fields, review `Honor Subject`, `Honor Key Usage`, `Honor Extended Key Usages` and `Honor Extensions`. The latter preserves SAN only, without validating entitlement to those names. Validity is not automatically clamped to CA expiration."},"2370":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For CA reissuance failures, check revocation and date: reissuance is not supported for a revoked or already expired CA. To change its key, use Hierarchy and rotation."},"2371":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Check each boundary independently:"},"2372":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Record:** read the correct certificate again by serial and issuer. Confirm status, reason and time; expired or permanently revoked records reject further transitions."},"2373":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Endpoint:** inspect AIA and CDP. Query those URLs from the consumer’s network; an old route or incorrect issuer can explain a discrepancy."},"2374":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**OCSP:** save a fresh response, verify signature and timestamps, and observe status. An HTTP error for an absent serial does not mean `Good` or guarantee a signed `Unknown`."},"2375":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**CRL:** compare `latest_crl`, number and timestamps with the downloaded list. Check the serial in its contents. If unchanged, review `regenerate_on_revoke`, event delivery, jobs, signing and storage with the deployment operator."},"2376":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Client:** check cache, policy for expired or unavailable evidence, critical IDP extension and rejection of a new connection."},"2377":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Reactivation from `CertificateHold` needs a new CRL for the client to stop seeing the hold. Reactivating a CA does not restore its descendant cascade; inspect every status and individual operation failure."},"2378":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"Check expected identity, SAN, KU/EKU, matching key, presented intermediates and consumer permissions. Distinguish server TLS trust, client authentication and action authorization. Follow Validation for positive and rejection tests."},"2379":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"When escalating a problem, provide identifiers, error and relevant public evidence, including query timestamps and version. This distinguishes issuance, publication and consumer application failures."},"2380":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"page","content":"3.8.0 to 4.0.0","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Upgrades"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0"},"2381":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-0","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","content":"4.0.0 changes that affect DMS configuration, what can break after upgrading from 3.8.0, and how to verify it."},"2382":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-1","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Summary"},"2383":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-2","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"DMS webhooks"},"2384":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-3","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"Webhooks with file references"},"2385":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-4","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#receiver-certificate-verification","content":"Receiver certificate verification"},"2386":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-5","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"Re-enrollment trust set"},"2387":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-6","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#independent-re-enrollment-authentication","content":"Independent re-enrollment authentication"},"2388":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-7","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"Verification checklist"},"2389":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-8","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","content":"Upgrading from 3.8.0 to 4.0.0 automatically migrates stored DMS configuration. Most of it converts without intervention, but three changes can leave enrollments failing or configs holding unexpected values if they are not reviewed. This page states what changes, what symptoms to expect and what to do in each case. Current behavior of each feature is documented in the DMS pages."},"2390":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-9","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Change"},"2391":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-10","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Who is affected"},"2392":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-11","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Severity"},"2393":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-12","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Action"},"2394":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-13","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Webhooks with file references"},"2395":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-14","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"DMSs with a webhook whose mTLS certificate or key were file paths"},"2396":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-15","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"High: enrollments and re-enrollments calling the webhook fail"},"2397":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-16","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Re-enter certificate and key as PEM, or remove the file fields"},"2398":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-17","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Receiver certificate verification"},"2399":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-18","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"DMSs with a webhook that had `validate_server_cert: false`"},"2400":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-19","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Medium: webhook credentials are sent to an unverified receiver"},"2401":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-20","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Set `insecure_skip_verify` to `false`"},"2402":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-21","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Re-enrollment trust set"},"2403":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-22","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Scripts and consoles that edit DMSs through the API"},"2404":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-23","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Medium: an edit in the old layout silently empties `validation_cas`"},"2405":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-24","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Read the DMS before editing and use the new field"},"2406":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-25","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Independent re-enrollment authentication"},"2407":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-26","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Any DMS"},"2408":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-27","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Low: informational"},"2409":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-28","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"Read both blocks before editing"},"2410":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-29","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#summary","content":"A verification checklist at the end confirms the result."},"2411":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-30","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Stored webhook configs are rewritten to the current layout. Fields are renamed as follows:"},"2412":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-31","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Field in 3.8.0"},"2413":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-32","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Field in 4.0.0"},"2414":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-33","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`validate_server_cert`"},"2415":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-34","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`insecure_skip_verify` (value negated)"},"2416":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-35","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`oidc`"},"2417":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-36","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`jwt_options`"},"2418":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-37","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`apikey`"},"2419":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-38","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`apikey_options`"},"2420":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-39","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`mtls`"},"2421":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-40","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`mtls_options`"},"2422":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-41","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"When the legacy mTLS certificate and key are both PEM, they move into `mtls_options.cert_content` and `mtls_options.key_content` and need no action. The two cases below do need it."},"2423":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-42","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"A mixed config, with a PEM certificate and a file-path key, is migrated to `mtls_options.cert_file` and `mtls_options.key_file`. Webhook delivery rejects those fields, and does so on every call, whatever the configured authentication mode. As a result, every enroll and re-enroll that calls that webhook fails until the config is fixed."},"2424":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-43","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"There are two ways to fix it, depending on the webhook:"},"2425":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-44","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"If the webhook uses mTLS, re-enter the certificate and key as Base64-encoded or plain PEM."},"2426":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-45","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"If the webhook does not use mTLS, remove the leftover file fields."},"2427":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-46","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"Metadata-only updates keep working in the meantime (`PUT` or `PATCH` on `/v1/dms/:id/metadata`)."},"2428":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-47","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#webhooks-with-file-references","content":"A variant of the same problem exists: if the stored config holds file paths inside `mtls_options.cert_content` or `mtls_options.key_content`, every full settings update (`POST /v1/dms` or `PUT /v1/dms/:id`) fails validation. Settings are replaced wholesale, so the stored config must be resent with the certificate and key as PEM."},"2429":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-48","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#receiver-certificate-verification","content":"A config with `validate_server_cert: false` becomes `insecure_skip_verify: true`. Receiver certificate verification therefore stays skipped until that field is set to `false`."},"2430":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-49","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#receiver-certificate-verification","content":"It should be corrected on every migrated config. The webhook authorization channel carries the API key or bearer token, so skipping verification exposes those credentials to a network-positioned attacker. Keeping `insecure_skip_verify: true` is only justified when the receiver certificate is deliberately unverifiable."},"2431":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-50","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"The flat field `reenrollment_settings.additional_validation_cas` moves into the nested field `reenrollment_settings.est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas`."},"2432":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-51","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"The effective trust set does not change, because the nested value was never consulted when validating re-enrollments. If the flat list was missing or null, it becomes an empty list."},"2433":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-52","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"What does change is how API requests are handled. Bodies that still carry `additional_validation_cas` are accepted, but the value is silently ignored because unknown JSON fields are dropped, and GET responses no longer include it. Consequently, an update body built from the old layout empties `validation_cas` without returning any error. To avoid it, always read the DMS before sending an edit and reuse the layout the API returns."},"2434":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-53","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#independent-re-enrollment-authentication","content":"Re-enrollment authentication settings are now stored independently from initial authentication. Nothing needs migrating, but both blocks should be read before editing a DMS so that one is not modified while believing the other is being edited."},"2435":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-54","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#independent-re-enrollment-authentication","content":"If the console version does not expose independent settings, they can be edited through the DMS API."},"2436":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-55","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"After applying the upgrade, check in this order:"},"2437":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-56","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"**Webhooks without file fields.** List the DMSs that use a webhook for enrollment or re-enrollment and confirm each `config` block carries `insecure_skip_verify` and the expected option block (`apikey_options`, `jwt_options` or `mtls_options`), with the certificate and key as PEM and no `cert_file` or `key_file`."},"2438":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-57","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"**Receiver verification.** Confirm `insecure_skip_verify` is `false`, unless the receiver certificate is intentionally unverified."},"2439":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-58","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"**Delivery.** Trigger, or wait for, one enroll or re-enroll through each migrated webhook and confirm the authorization call completes."},"2440":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-59","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"**Trust set.** Read `est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas` and confirm it holds the expected CAs, in particular those of the old CA during rotation overlaps."},"2441":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-60","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"**API clients.** Update any script or console that uses the old DMS layout (flat `additional_validation_cas`, or the legacy `mtls`, `apikey` and `oidc` fields), since they silently drop those values."},"2442":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-61","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"<Card title=\"Configure a DMS\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms\" />"},"2443":{"id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-62","page_id":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#verification-checklist","content":"<Card title=\"DMS API\" href=\"/docs/api-reference/dms-manager\" />"}},"count":2443},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":901,"2":1834,"3":610,"4":1286,"5":1545,"6":772,"7":1429,"8":1427,"9":1482,"10":2008,"11":1589,"12":466,"13":453,"14":43,"15":148,"16":109,"17":1168,"18":1860,"19":774,"20":1925,"21":809,"22":902,"23":741,"24":723,"25":1368,"26":491,"27":2420,"28":1473,"29":1710,"30":2394,"31":1931,"32":1396,"33":1656,"34":2441,"35":