thorization."],[830,"Verify the endpoints"],[1685,"Verify the import"],[89,"Verify the installation"],[1445,"Verify the obtained identity"],[751,"Verify the registration"],[1867,"Verify the request with `openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`. Review subject, SAN and algorithm, and authorize the requested identity."],[2232,"Verify the result"],[2270,"Verify the result"],[2184,"Verify the returned DER:"],[254,"Verify the traffic path"],[1814,"Verify these criteria together:"],[57,"Version upgrades."],[2039,"View details"],[2330,"We use `Acme Evaluation Root CA` and `device-001` as example names. If you replace them, keep the same client identifier in the steps you want to connect."],[878,"Webhook and combined modes also execute during re-enrollment when configured in its block. They do not implicitly degrade to NO\\_AUTH. An absent or unrecognized mode fails."],[804,"Webhook contract"],[911,"Webhook credentials must be stored as PEM content. File references (`ca_cert_file`, `mtls_options.cert_file`, `mtls_options.key_file`) are never valid in a stored webhook config: delivery rejects any webhook config that references files, whatever its auth mode, so every enroll and reenroll that calls that webhook fails until the certificate and key are entered as Base64-encoded or plain PEM in `mtls_options.cert_content` and `key_content`, or the file fields are removed if the webhook does not use mTLS. If a stored config holds file paths in `mtls_options.cert_content` or `key_content`, every full settings update (`POST /v1/dms`, `PUT /v1/dms/:id`) fails validation — settings are replaced wholesale, so the stored config must be resent — until the values are replaced by PEM content or the webhook stops being used. Meanwhile, delivery of that webhook fails on every call; a metadata-only update through `PUT` or `PATCH` on `/v1/dms/:id/metadata` still succeeds. If your stored config previously relied on `validate_server_cert: false`, it now carries `insecure_skip_verify: true`: receiver-certificate verification stays skipped until you set that flag to `false`. See 3.8.0 to 4.0.0 for the upgrade notes and the operator checklist."],[616,"Webhook delivery rules"],[1134,"Webhook denies, times out or responds without authorization"],[2384,"Webhooks with file references"],[2394,"Webhooks with file references"],[1748,"What a profile controls"],[661,"What an event contains"],[1180,"What cacerts returns"],[1929,"What can be issued"],[2433,"What does change is how API requests are handled. Bodies that still carry `additional_validation_cas` are accepted, but the value is silently ignored because unknown JSON fields are dropped, and GET responses no longer include it. Consequently, an update body built from the old layout empties `validation_cas` without returning any error. To avoid it, always read the DMS before sending an edit and reuse the layout the API returns."],[80,"What Fastlane adds"],[252,"What if you need three Gateways?"],[326,"What it installs"],[1608,"What it prepares or checks"],[1406,"What it represents"],[1225,"What the connector writes to the shadow"],[2026,"What the KMS solves"],[319,"What the Lamassu chart provides"],[86,"What the script configures"],[51,"What the service manages"],[1048,"What to check"],[1125,"What to check"],[2352,"What to inspect"],[2299,"What to review"],[1583,"What you manage"],[1832,"What you must maintain"],[2195,"What you need"],[1895,"What you should watch"],[1323,"When `primary_account` is `false`, the connector registers the CA using `CertificateMode: SNI_ONLY`. This mode requires no verification code or access to the CA's private key, so it is the right choice when the CA is managed from another AWS account or when the administrator does not hold the private key. It is the usual method to register the same CA in several AWS accounts simultaneously."],[2091,"When an existing PKI needs to be migrated without reissuing certificates."],[2379,"When escalating a problem, provide identifiers, error and